<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Idris I al-Mamun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">renounced Ibn Tumart's Mahdi status 1229</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as al-Mamun, Idris I al-Ma'mun, Idris I al-Ma</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Idris I al-Mamun was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> of the early thirteenth century. In 1229 he renounced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-tumart">Ibn Tumart</a>'s status as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a>, abandoning a founding doctrine of the Almohad movement. The step damaged the ideological basis of the Almohad Caliphate during its decline.</p></div>
